---
import PrivacyActions from '../components/PrivacyActions';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy & Local Data Boundary | teleprompter.wtf';
const description =
  'A plain-language account of how teleprompter.wtf handles scripts, microphone audio, local voice models, recordings, storage, and optional usage analytics.';
const schema = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://www.teleprompter.wtf/' },
      {
        '@type': 'ListItem',
        position: 2,
        name: 'Privacy',
        item: 'https://www.teleprompter.wtf/privacy',
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <article class="prose-page section-wrap">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Privacy</span>
    </nav>
    <header class="page-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">Plain-language privacy</p>
      <h1>Your script, voice, and recordings stay on your device.</h1>
      <p>
        The teleprompter processes and displays your words on your device. We designed the core tool
        so it does not need to receive them. Optional site measurement is separate and off until you
        choose it.
      </p>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 23 August 2026</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose-grid">
      <aside class="privacy-summary" aria-label="Privacy summary">
        <strong>In one minute</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>No account or login</li>
          <li>No script upload</li>
          <li>No speech or audio upload</li>
          <li>No recording upload</li>
          <li>Optional measurement only after explicit consent</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose-body">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <div
          class="privacy-table-wrap"
          role="region"
          aria-label="Privacy data handling table"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          <table class="privacy-table">
            <thead
              ><tr
                ><th>Data</th><th>Used for</th><th>Processed where</th><th>Persisted where</th><th
                  >Sent externally</th
                ></tr
              ></thead
            >
            <tbody>
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Script</th><td>Editing and presenting</td><td>Browser</td><td
                  >Local storage when autosave is available</td
                ><td>No</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Preferences</th><td>Presenter setup</td><td>Browser</td><td
                  >Local storage</td
                ><td>No</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Manual Mode</th><td>Elapsed-time scroll</td><td>Browser</td><td
                  >Nowhere</td
                ><td>No</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Smart Pace microphone</th><td>Speech cadence & rhythm</td><td
                  >Browser Web Audio</td
                ><td>Nowhere (in-memory signal only)</td><td>No</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Private Precision microphone</th><td>Local speech alignment</td><td
                  >Browser Web Worker</td
                ><td>Nowhere (in-memory PCM only)</td><td>No</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Recognition fragments</th><td>Local script alignment</td><td
                  >Browser Web Worker</td
                ><td>Nowhere (transient in-memory text)</td><td>No</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Voice model</th><td>Local recognition</td><td>Browser</td><td
                  >Versioned Cache Storage</td
                ><td>Downloaded from teleprompter.wtf on user opt-in only</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Recordings</th><td>Local capture and preview</td><td
                  >Browser MediaRecorder</td
                ><td>In-memory Blob; saved only when you download the file</td><td>No</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">Umami events</th><td>Aggregate product usage</td><td
                  >Self-hosted Umami at analytics.sabya.pm, only after opt-in</td
                ><td>According to operator settings</td><td>Yes, after analytics consent</td></tr
              >
              <tr
                ><th scope="row">GA4 events</th><td>Aggregate product usage</td><td
                  >Google Analytics, only after opt-in when configured</td
                ><td>According to operator and Google settings</td><td
                  >Yes, after analytics consent</td
                ></tr
              >
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <h2>Script processing</h2>
        <p>
          Your script stays in your browser. Script contents are not added to the page URL, sent to
          teleprompter.wtf, included in analytics events, or intentionally written to application
          logs.
        </p>
        <h2>Local browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          To restore your work after a refresh, the tool may save your script and preferences in
          your browser’s local storage. That data remains associated with this browser profile on
          this device. It is not synchronization and will not appear on another device.
        </p>
        <p>
          Anyone with access to your unlocked browser profile may be able to access locally stored
          data. Clear the script after working with sensitive material, use a private browsing
          window, or use the control below to remove all data owned by teleprompter.wtf.
        </p>
        <PrivacyActions client:load />
        <h2>Microphone and local voice tracking</h2>
        <p>
          The microphone is requested only after you start presenting with a voice mode selected.
          Smart Pace listens locally: it analyzes signal energy and cadence in this browser using
          Web Audio and does not transcribe your voice. Private Precision Beta runs a Whisper speech
          model on your device to find your place in the known script, using temporary recognition
          fragments that never leave the device. Stopping voice tracking or leaving the presenter
          stops media tracks, closes the audio context, and disposes of local recognition state.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Private Precision model is downloaded once, on your explicit request, and kept in this
          browser for future visits. The first download transfers about 67 MB in total: 45 MB of
          model files served from teleprompter.wtf, plus the ONNX WASM runtime fetched at first use.
          The model is stored in versioned browser Cache Storage and is removable without deleting
          your script.
        </p>
        <h2>Local recording</h2>
        <p>
          Screen and camera capture use browser media APIs (getDisplayMedia and getUserMedia).
          Recordings are created locally and are not uploaded: recorded chunks become a local Blob
          for preview and direct file saving. The application has no recording endpoint and does not
          persist a recording unless you choose to save the file.
        </p>
        <h2>Optional usage analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Optional usage analytics measure product usage with your consent. It is a single,
          unchecked choice: no analytics script is loaded before you allow it, No thanks is given
          equal prominence, and the teleprompter works identically either way. You can reopen
          Privacy choices on the homepage and withdraw consent at any time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Self-hosted Umami (analytics.sabya.pm) records page views and a fixed vocabulary of
          low-cardinality product events. Google Analytics 4 is included only when the operator
          configures a measurement ID. Neither receives your script or voice content. When GA4 is
          present, advertising storage, ad user data, ad personalization, and Google signals stay
          denied. Events never include script text, recognition fragments, filenames, microphone
          labels, clipboard contents, or raw error messages.
        </p>
        <h2>Network requests</h2>
        <p>
          Loading the website necessarily reveals ordinary request information to the hosting
          provider, such as an IP address, user agent, and requested page. The core teleprompter
          requires no network request containing your script.
        </p>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can decline optional analytics, clear the current script, clear saved preferences,
          remove the local voice model, or configure the browser to block storage. Clearing all site
          data through browser settings removes both local app data and model caches.
        </p>
        <h2>Questions and changes</h2>
        <p>
          This policy will be updated when the product’s data practices change. Questions or privacy
          issues can be raised in the project’s <a
            href="https://github.com/SABYA648/Telemprompter-WTF/issues"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">public issue tracker</a
          >; do not include private script content.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
